<Song resolves-to="SongSP" spName="ItCouldHappenToYou-Bb-Theme" spTempo="142">
  <spVERSION>4</spVERSION>
  <spComments>Year:	1936
Composer:	Isham Jones
Lyricist:	Marty Symes
Form:	32-bar ABAC
Style:	Swing; often performed as a ballad or at a
	medium-up tempo
Key:	Bb major

Isham Jones and His Orchestra introduced the song
in 1936, with Woody Herman singing; it was released
as the B-side of “Life Begins When You’re in Love.”
The tune became a jazz standard, with notable
performances ranging from Dinah Washington’s ballad
version to swinging recordings by Miles Davis.</spComments>
